```

## Performance Checklist

Before committing performance-sensitive code:
- [ ] No allocations in `_process()` or `_physics_process()`
- [ ] All entities use object pooling (bullets, enemies, particles)
- [ ] Node references are cached (no repeated `get_node()`)
- [ ] Groups are cached (no `get_nodes_in_group()` in hot paths)
- [ ] Rate limiters prevent spawn spikes
- [ ] Graceful degradation under high load
- [ ] Integer math used for counters and indices
- [ ] Trigonometry pre-calculated or cached
- [ ] Distance checks use `distance_squared_to()` when possible
- [ ] Shader operations minimized per-pixel
- [ ] Particle systems use GPU particles (>20 particles)
- [ ] Debug code is gated behind constants
- [ ] Profiled with 500+ bullets on screen
- [ ] Maintains 60 FPS during stress test

